  "worked_solution": "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & \u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+3{x}_{3}=0\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=-3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$",
